{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554321-is-augustus-giovanni-really-that-fat","id":1554321,"title":"Is Augustus Giovanni really that fat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-12T14:34:28-07:00","id":1554321,"title":"Is Augustus Giovanni really that fat?","content":"This is something that often becomes a major topic in our conversations, how fat is Augustus Giovanni? There's a portrait of him (in GC if I'm not mistaken) where he appears to be really fat.<br /> And for the matter, do you believe he was really diablerised? And if so, by whom? Is Lazarus the new Antediluvian? Or the Capuchin (I mean, how the &quot;entity&quot; is described in V20, perhaps?)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T16:47:03-07:00","id":1554327,"title":"","content":"This is the picture from CG:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"Giovanni\" width=\"300\" height=\"171\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/e/ec/Augustus_CbG.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20140428232553\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/e/ec/Augustus_CbG.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20140428232553\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/e/ec/Augustus_CbG.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20140428232553\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Giovanni\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> This is the first depiction of him that I have seen and it\u2019s personally how I picture him. Not a pretty boy like we often see from vampires, more unique.<br /> <br /> As for still being undead? In my personal headcanon, he never diablerized Cappadocians and is 4th generation - though he\u2019s still (un)alive in my headcanon as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T18:08:44-07:00","id":1554328,"title":"","content":"Not Mocada fat, but just fat.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T19:33:12-07:00","id":1554330,"title":"","content":"Well, at least he's somehow got a picture. Better than Goratrix that always appears with a hood (even though his description usually say he's handsome, his character sheet has 2 in appearance and from what I remember he's always pictured with a hood, quite disappointing!) or Tremere that we're never sure how he looks like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T21:13:35-07:00","id":1554331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554321-is-augustus-giovanni-really-that-fat?p=1554330#post1554330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, at least he's somehow got a picture. Better than Goratrix that always appears with a hood (even though his description usually say he's handsome, his character sheet has 2 in appearance and from what I remember he's always pictured with a hood, quite disappointing!) or Tremere that we're never sure how he looks like...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was Goratrix's stats? Transylvania Chronicles? I never recall seeing that.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T21:14:48-07:00","id":1554332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554321-is-augustus-giovanni-really-that-fat?p=1554331#post1554331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where was Goratrix's stats? Transylvania Chronicles? I never recall seeing that.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages France. Onee of the most beautiful books ever released, leider wasn't translated to English.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T22:57:23-07:00","id":1554333,"title":"","content":"Since we are speaking of the patriarch in the 50s-60s of a medieval merchant family in early 11th century, portly might be a more apt word perhaps.<br /> <br /> It's a time where people of delicate physique hardly get to live long and sometimes merchants had to travel alongside their entrerprises for weeks, when not months or years between countries and even continents. Definitely big-boned, but in no way soft or obese.<br /> <br /> He's also most entertained in contemporary times by the doge meme and has occasionally invested in the cryptocurrency market. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Goratrix i tend to envision like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Al-Aswad</a>, due to how &quot;Black Man of witches' sabbats&quot; imagery seem to figure strongly in the portrayal of both characters - though i'd say Goratrix is more medieval pagan/neodruid (perhaps a house Diedne rogue before becoming Tremere) than satanic/nephandi per se.<br /> <br /> (I also think there might be a mention about him being blond in his description on Transylvania Chronicles 1 or 2?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2025, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T23:34:34-07:00","id":1554334,"title":"","content":"Hard to tell<br /> The TCG is a very nice picture<br /> In the Giovanni clanbook? Not that much, even with an appearance 4<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/esrAMZ3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/esrAMZ3\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/esrAMZ3\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/a/esrAMZ3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T00:22:50-07:00","id":1554336,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554321-is-augustus-giovanni-really-that-fat?p=1554327#post1554327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the picture from CG:<br /> In my personal headcanon, he never diablerized Cappadocians and is 4th generation - though he\u2019s still (un)alive in my headcanon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is strongly hinted Augustus is still 4th generation<br /> Simply, there are no 4th Generation Giovanni... for some reason he simply stopped to Embrace after becoming supposedly becoming 3rd Generation<br /> Sure, Vampire is full of holes when it comes to geneology, but you can trace most of the vampires<br /> But for the Giovanni?<br /> Claudius Giovanni from Giovanni Chronicles I: The Last Supper is Augustus only Child we know of for certain, Embraced in 1035 CE - and since Cappadocius was presumably been embraced in April 12, 1444? Yeah his is firmly 5th (and I think the book also put him in 5th)<br /> There is another Progeny of His, Ignazio Giovanni from Clanbook: Cappadocian; no date of Embrace nor Generation is given but &quot;he was among the first members of the Giovanni bloodline back in the days when the Clan was considered a branch of the Cappadocians&quot; suggesting he is also a 5th Generation<br /> <br /> There is Andreas Giovanni from Chaos Factor who is the 5th Genration Child of Claudius Giovanni, and his kid, Lisandro Giovanni is 6th Generation<br /> Andreas' date of Embrace is unknown... but, since his Sire, Claudius Giovanni was Embraced in to the 5th Generation? It only proves Claudius ate his way up in to the 4th Generation, quite a feat, considering not may 4th Generation Cappadocian was running around between 1035 and 1444... namely? Caias (who may or may not dead) Japheth, Humuusa, Byzar/Mahatma and Lazarus + any unnamed kids of Cappadocius. Whoever he managed to nail is a mystery but supposedly it is Japheth and indeed Japheth became a Wraith but also there is Unre, his Child who got trapped in the Underworld afetr ~300 of persecution from the Giovanni but was able to contact her sire across the veil of death... suggesting Japeth was alive to help her perform the ritual that would free the Harbringers from their unholy entrapment. But in V20 Japeth was a Wraith for over five centuries and amassed enough knowledge of the geography of the Underworld that he rivals even the Ferryman<br /> (So... we have again a nice little anomaly, either Claudius ate him or not, but if he got his hand on Japeth then like with Augustus, we have a Diableire with an escaped soul that became a Wraith. If he avoided to become a meal altogether, then he probably &quot;ascended&quot; to become a Wraith later to make sense of his V20 state of existance) \u200b<br /> <br /> Every publiced and known Giovanni is 5th or above<br /> <br /> There are a few &quot;rules&quot; but Amaranth is one of them<br /> It is quite &quot;simple&quot;, you have to consume another Kindred's vitae to the point of Final Death, then continnue, the soul is consumed with the vampire's heart's blood<br /> Diablerizing the soul of a Cainite of significant age is one of the few ways of lowering one's generation<br /> So you have to feast on the soul, not just the blood<br /> In the 2002 Dark Ages: Vampire Rulebook it was detailed what the hell is that heart's blood we heard about for a decade then refined in Vampire Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Dark Ages,<br /> <br /> &quot;Assamite studies of vitae have isolated the part within a vampire's blood that contains the soul. They call it &quot;heart's blood&quot; and it manifests as a thick, blackish liquid that quickly grows dry when it leaves the body.<br /> Via applications of Quietus, they are able to manipulate the heart's blood to allow them to diablerize a victim later.<br /> Furthermore, studies in Quietus have found a way to force the last drop of vitae within a vampire's body to calcify the heart into a semi-translucent grayish-white flask known as a &quot;Debitum&quot;. The Debitum enshrouds the spiritual essence (the &quot;heart's-blood&quot;) of the victim \u2013 which, if examined in detail, can be seen encased within, swimming in despair. Heart\u2019s-blood preserved in this way endures indefinitely.<br /> If vampiric fangs pierce it, the heart reanimates, pumping a cupful of celadon-colored, aqueous, non-burning flame vaguely resembling the victim into the vampire's maw.<br /> The vampire gains all the benefits of diablerie from this.&quot;<br /> <br /> And if anything we know a Cappadocius escaped to be a Wraith - it is even stated, Augustus Giovanni did not manage to absorb his soul during the diablerie<br /> Which is... uhm... the point of the Diableire?<br /> <br /> My personal headcannon is, the True Vessel, the jar with Cappadocius' blood he used in the Embrace of Augustus contained the Ancient's Heart's Blood - Alamut is somewhere in Afghanistan, Mount Erciyes is in Turkey and it is funny to think Cappadocius visited Haqim to learn some Quietus - and became his strongest and most important Fetter and the Giovanni Family's greatest secret is a the fact their &quot;Antediluvian&quot; is a fraud<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T04:27:20-07:00","id":1554340,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"800\" height=\"1110\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/07/05/61/07056183d51e8e627ee0b3871784fa83.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/07/05/61/07056183d51e8e627ee0b3871784fa83.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/07/05/61/07056183d51e8e627ee0b3871784fa83.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Augustus Giovanni by Raquel Cornejo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T09:45:18-07:00","id":1554345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554321-is-augustus-giovanni-really-that-fat?p=1554332#post1554332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Ages France. Onee of the most beautiful books ever released, leider wasn't translated to English.</div> </div> </div> </div>I translated it for Arkhane Asylum (this one and the Cathar Heresy book) but they were never released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T18:27:08-07:00","id":1554355,"title":"","content":"Regardless of anything in the books, I always pictured him as William Hickey's character in <i>Prizzi's Honor.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":